# Text is stored as LF and checked out as LF everywhere, Windows included.
#
# This project has already been bitten by the alternative. `normalize_newlines`
# in `scripts/arxiv_backend.py` exists because a CRLF that survives into
# pandoc's output gets written as `\r\r\n`, which reads back as a blank line —
# and a blank line inside `$$` display maths terminates the formula, so the
# prose after it is swallowed as maths. CI runs on Ubuntu; a working copy that
# differs from CI in line endings is a class of bug nobody needs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Archives and images. Never convert these.
*.epub binary
*.zip  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.docx binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
